# Lead-lens sign-off — harness gates the publish
- date: 2026-11-05
- branch: fix/harness-gates-publish
- lead: michael-nygard
- findings-cleared:
  - No RED on the change itself — it moves an existing check, and the check
    was proven green in the parent PR (12 of 12, both scenarios).
  - Caught while writing it: ADR-004's ordered-steps list has drifted from
    the workflow. It says Node 20 where publish.yml uses Node 22, and omits
    five steps that exist (pin read, mirror checkout, pin assert, dist/lite
    bundle, six-file floor). Named in the amendment rather than reconciled,
    because fixing the whole list is a separate change. Adding a thirteenth
    line to a list that misdescribes twelve would have been worse.
  - Caught while writing it: the published scenario cannot run pre-publish —
    the version is not on the registry, so it would fail on infrastructure
    rather than on the package. HARNESS_INCLUDE_PUBLISHED stays unset in the
    checks job; harness.yml still runs both after release.
- verification: publish.yml parses; the harness is step 17, last in checks;
  job 2 still declares needs: checks and environment: npm-publish, so the
  order is pack-and-run, then human gate, then publish.
- lens-verdict: PASS, with the limit stated. A failure can now stop a
  publish, which is what the lens asks. Full proof needs a real release —
  nothing here exercises the gate end to end, and I have not pretended
  otherwise.
- iteration_count: 1
- wu_id: harness repair, step 2 of the sequence
- lens_used: [michael-nygard, tony-hoare, saltzer-schroeder]
